IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `ccc-core`
IMPORT `ccc12-logic`

-- ccc12-part9-criminal-interest.l4 -- Criminal Code (Canada), Part IX, "Criminal Interest Rate": sections 347 to 347.1.
-- Source: a plain-text rendering, made by a converter script, of the Justice Laws Website consolidation (current to 2026-09-30); not the official text.
-- Reading a result: see the header of ccc12-part9-theft.l4 and NOTES.md ("Reading a result: FALSE and NOTHING (ccc12)").
-- Money is a NUMBER of dollars; a rate is a NUMBER of per cent (35 means 35 per cent). Amounts, rates and limits the text leaves to regulations (s 347.01, s 347.1(2.1)),
-- to the Bank Act, the Interest Act, the Tax Rebate Discounting Act or to a designation by order (s 347.1(3)) are INPUTS, never numbers from memory.

§ `Criminal Interest Rate (ss 347 to 347.1)`

§§ `Section 347(1) -- the offence`

-- src:6798 | Criminal interest rate
-- src:6799 | 347 (1) Despite any other Act of Parliament, every person who enters or offers to enter into an agreement or arrangement to receive interest at a criminal rate, who advertises an offer to enter into an agreement or arrangement that provides for the receipt of interest at a criminal rate or who receives a payment or partial payment of interest at a criminal rate is
-- src:6800 | (a) guilty of an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term not exceeding five years; or
-- src:6801 | (b) guilty of an offence punishable on summary conviction and liable to a fine of not more than $25,000 or to imprisonment for a term of not more than two years less a day, or to both.
@ref Criminal Code s 347(1) (src:6798-6801)
GIVEN `the rate is a criminal rate, by s 347(2) the rate is a criminal rate` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person enters or offers to enter into an agreement or arrangement to receive interest` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person advertises an offer to enter into an agreement or arrangement that provides for the receipt of interest` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person receives a payment or partial payment of interest` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 347(1) the person commits the offence of receiving interest at a criminal rate` MEANS
    `ccc12 and` `the rate is a criminal rate, by s 347(2) the rate is a criminal rate`
                (JUST (    `the person enters or offers to enter into an agreement or arrangement to receive interest`
                        OR `the person advertises an offer to enter into an agreement or arrangement that provides for the receipt of interest`
                        OR `the person receives a payment or partial payment of interest`))
    -- JUST FALSE where the rate is a definite no or no act holds: FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "every person who enters or offers to enter into an agreement or arrangement to receive interest at a criminal rate, who advertises an offer to enter into an agreement or arrangement that provides for the receipt of interest at a criminal rate or who receives a payment or partial payment of interest at a criminal rate"
    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): where the answer of subsection (2), "criminal rate", was not given

-- (a) indictable, not exceeding five years; (b) summary: a fine of not more than $25,000 or imprisonment of not more than two years less a day, or both. Both limbs are stated by the section itself, so no input is needed.
@ref Criminal Code s 347(1) (src:6799-6801)
GIVETH A LIST OF Punishment
`s 347(1) the punishment for the offence` MEANS
    LIST `ccc12 an indictable limb` (`imprisonment for a term of` `five years`)   -- (a) guilty of an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term not exceeding five years
       , Punishment WITH
             `mode` IS `on summary conviction`   -- (b) guilty of an offence punishable on summary conviction ...
             `maximum imprisonment` IS `imprisonment for a term of` `two years less a day`   -- ... or to imprisonment for a term of not more than two years less a day
             `minimum imprisonment` IS `no imprisonment is stated`
             `maximum fine` IS `a fine of` 25000   -- ... and liable to a fine of not more than $25,000 or to imprisonment ..., or to both
             `minimum fine` IS `no fine is stated`

§§ `Section 347(2) -- definitions`

-- credit advanced means the aggregate of the money and the monetary value of any goods, services or benefits actually advanced or to be advanced, minus the aggregate of any required deposit balance and any fee, fine, penalty, commission and other similar charge or expense incurred under the original or any collateral agreement.
-- src:6804 | credit advanced means the aggregate of the money and the monetary value of any goods, services or benefits actually advanced or to be advanced under an agreement or arrangement, or that would be advanced if an agreement or arrangement — as offered, including in an advertisement — was entered into, minus the aggregate of any required deposit balance and any fee, fine, penalty, commission and other similar charge or expense directly or indirectly incurred under the original or any collateral agreement or arrangement; (capital prêté)
@ref Criminal Code s 347(2) credit advanced (src:6804)
GIVEN `the money actually advanced or to be advanced, in dollars` IS A NUMBER
      `the monetary value of any goods, services or benefits actually advanced or to be advanced, in dollars` IS A NUMBER
      `the aggregate of any required deposit balance, in dollars` IS A NUMBER
      `the aggregate of any fee, fine, penalty, commission and other similar charge or expense directly or indirectly incurred under the original or any collateral agreement or arrangement, in dollars` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 347(2) credit advanced` MEANS
    (`the money actually advanced or to be advanced, in dollars` PLUS `the monetary value of any goods, services or benefits actually advanced or to be advanced, in dollars`)
    MINUS (`the aggregate of any required deposit balance, in dollars` PLUS `the aggregate of any fee, fine, penalty, commission and other similar charge or expense directly or indirectly incurred under the original or any collateral agreement or arrangement, in dollars`)

-- criminal rate means an annual percentage rate of interest calculated in accordance with generally accepted actuarial practices and principles that exceeds 35 per cent on the credit advanced.
-- src:6805 | criminal rate means an annual percentage rate of interest calculated in accordance with generally accepted actuarial practices and principles that exceeds 35 per cent on the credit advanced; (taux criminel)
@ref Criminal Code s 347(2) criminal rate (src:6805)
GIVEN `the annual percentage rate of interest on the credit advanced, in per cent` IS A NUMBER
      `the rate was calculated in accordance with generally accepted actuarial practices and principles` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 347(2) the rate is a criminal rate` MEANS
    IF `the rate was calculated in accordance with generally accepted actuarial practices and principles` AND `the annual percentage rate of interest on the credit advanced, in per cent` GREATER THAN 35
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "criminal rate means an annual percentage rate of interest calculated in accordance with generally accepted actuarial practices and principles that exceeds 35 per cent on the credit advanced"

-- insurance charge means the cost of insuring the risk assumed by the person who advances or is to advance credit, where the face amount of the insurance does not exceed the credit advanced.
-- src:6806 | insurance charge means the cost of insuring the risk assumed by the person who advances or is to advance credit under an agreement or arrangement, where the face amount of the insurance does not exceed the credit advanced; (frais d’assurance)
@ref Criminal Code s 347(2) insurance charge (src:6806)
GIVEN `it is the cost of insuring the risk assumed by the person who advances or is to advance credit under the agreement or arrangement` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the face amount of the insurance, in dollars` IS A NUMBER
      `the credit advanced, in dollars` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 347(2) the cost is an insurance charge` MEANS
    IF `it is the cost of insuring the risk assumed by the person who advances or is to advance credit under the agreement or arrangement` AND `the face amount of the insurance, in dollars` AT MOST `the credit advanced, in dollars`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "insurance charge means the cost of insuring the risk assumed by the person who advances or is to advance credit under an agreement or arrangement, where the face amount of the insurance does not exceed the credit advanced"

-- interest means the aggregate of all charges and expenses ... paid or payable for the advancing of credit, but does not include any repayment of credit advanced or any insurance charge, official fee, overdraft charge, required deposit balance or, in a mortgage or hypothec transaction, any amount required to be paid on account of property taxes.
-- Each excluded kind is asked as the part of the aggregate that is of that kind (an assumption: the excluded amounts are included in the aggregate; fork F-INTEREST).
-- src:6807 | interest means the aggregate of all charges and expenses, whether in the form of a fee, fine, penalty, commission or other similar charge or expense or in any other form, paid or payable for the advancing of credit under an agreement or arrangement, or that would be paid or payable if such an agreement or arrangement was entered into, by or on behalf of the person to whom the credit is or is to be advanced, or would be advanced, irrespective of the person to whom any such charges and expenses are or are to be paid or payable, or would be paid or payable, but does not include any repayment of credit advanced or any insurance charge, official fee, overdraft charge, required deposit balance or, in the case of a mortgage or hypothec transaction, any amount required to be paid on account of property taxes; (intérêt)
@ref Criminal Code s 347(2) interest (src:6807)
GIVEN `the aggregate of all charges and expenses, in any form, paid or payable for the advancing of credit under the agreement or arrangement, in dollars` IS A NUMBER
      `the part of it that is repayment of credit advanced, in dollars` IS A NUMBER
      `the part of it that is an insurance charge, in dollars` IS A NUMBER
      `the part of it that is an official fee, in dollars` IS A NUMBER
      `the part of it that is an overdraft charge, in dollars` IS A NUMBER
      `the part of it that is a required deposit balance, in dollars` IS A NUMBER
      `the transaction is a mortgage or hypothec transaction` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the part of it that is an amount required to be paid on account of property taxes, in dollars` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 347(2) interest` MEANS
    `the aggregate of all charges and expenses, in any form, paid or payable for the advancing of credit under the agreement or arrangement, in dollars`
    MINUS (   `the part of it that is repayment of credit advanced, in dollars`
         PLUS `the part of it that is an insurance charge, in dollars`
         PLUS `the part of it that is an official fee, in dollars`
         PLUS `the part of it that is an overdraft charge, in dollars`
         PLUS `the part of it that is a required deposit balance, in dollars`
         PLUS (IF `the transaction is a mortgage or hypothec transaction` THEN `the part of it that is an amount required to be paid on account of property taxes, in dollars` ELSE 0))

-- official fee means a fee required by law to be paid to any governmental authority in connection with perfecting any security under an agreement or arrangement for the advancing of credit.
-- src:6808 | official fee means a fee required by law to be paid to any governmental authority in connection with perfecting any security under an agreement or arrangement for the advancing of credit; (taxe officielle)
@ref Criminal Code s 347(2) official fee (src:6808)
GIVEN `it is a fee required by law` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is to be paid to a governmental authority` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is in connection with perfecting any security under an agreement or arrangement for the advancing of credit` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 347(2) the fee is an official fee` MEANS
    IF `it is a fee required by law` AND `it is to be paid to a governmental authority` AND `it is in connection with perfecting any security under an agreement or arrangement for the advancing of credit`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "official fee means a fee required by law to be paid to any governmental authority in connection with perfecting any security under an agreement or arrangement for the advancing of credit"

-- overdraft charge means a charge not exceeding five dollars for the creation of or increase in an overdraft, imposed by a credit union or caisse populaire (members wholly or substantially natural persons) or a deposit taking institution (deposits insured by the CDIC or guaranteed by the Quebec Deposit Insurance Board).
-- src:6809 | overdraft charge means a charge not exceeding five dollars for the creation of or increase in an overdraft, imposed by a credit union or caisse populaire the membership of which is wholly or substantially comprised of natural persons or a deposit taking institution the deposits in which are insured, in whole or in part, by the Canada Deposit Insurance Corporation or guaranteed, in whole or in part, by the Quebec Deposit Insurance Board; (frais pour découvert de compte)
@ref Criminal Code s 347(2) overdraft charge (src:6809)
GIVEN `the amount of the charge, in dollars` IS A NUMBER
      `it is for the creation of or increase in an overdraft` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is imposed by a credit union or caisse populaire the membership of which is wholly or substantially comprised of natural persons` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is imposed by a deposit taking institution the deposits in which are insured, in whole or in part, by the Canada Deposit Insurance Corporation or guaranteed, in whole or in part, by the Quebec Deposit Insurance Board` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 347(2) the charge is an overdraft charge` MEANS
    IF    `the amount of the charge, in dollars` AT MOST 5
      AND `it is for the creation of or increase in an overdraft`
      AND (   `it is imposed by a credit union or caisse populaire the membership of which is wholly or substantially comprised of natural persons`
           OR `it is imposed by a deposit taking institution the deposits in which are insured, in whole or in part, by the Canada Deposit Insurance Corporation or guaranteed, in whole or in part, by the Quebec Deposit Insurance Board`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "overdraft charge means a charge not exceeding five dollars for the creation of or increase in an overdraft"

-- required deposit balance means a fixed or ascertainable amount of the money actually advanced or to be advanced that is required, as a condition, to be deposited or invested by or on behalf of the person to whom the advance is made and that may be available, on default, to or for the benefit of the person who advances the money.
-- src:6810 | required deposit balance means a fixed or an ascertainable amount of the money actually advanced or to be advanced under an agreement or arrangement that is required, as a condition of the agreement or arrangement, to be deposited or invested by or on behalf of the person to whom the advance is or is to be made and that may be available, in the event of his defaulting in any payment, to or for the benefit of the person who advances or is to advance the money. (dépôt de garantie)
@ref Criminal Code s 347(2) required deposit balance (src:6810)
GIVEN `it is a fixed or an ascertainable amount of the money actually advanced or to be advanced under an agreement or arrangement` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is required, as a condition of the agreement or arrangement, to be deposited or invested by or on behalf of the person to whom the advance is or is to be made` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it may be available, in the event of that person defaulting in any payment, to or for the benefit of the person who advances or is to advance the money` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 347(2) the amount is a required deposit balance` MEANS
    IF    `it is a fixed or an ascertainable amount of the money actually advanced or to be advanced under an agreement or arrangement`
      AND `it is required, as a condition of the agreement or arrangement, to be deposited or invested by or on behalf of the person to whom the advance is or is to be made`
      AND `it may be available, in the event of that person defaulting in any payment, to or for the benefit of the person who advances or is to advance the money`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "required deposit balance means a fixed or an ascertainable amount of the money actually advanced or to be advanced under an agreement or arrangement that is required, as a condition of the agreement or arrangement, to be deposited or invested"

§§ `Section 347(3) to (8) -- presumption, proof, notice, cross-examination, application`

-- src:6811 | Presumption
-- src:6812 | (3) Where a person receives a payment or partial payment of interest at a criminal rate, he shall, in the absence of evidence to the contrary, be deemed to have knowledge of the nature of the payment and that it was received at a criminal rate.
@ref Criminal Code s 347(3) (src:6811-6812)
GIVEN `the person receives a payment or partial payment of interest at a criminal rate` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there is evidence to the contrary` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 347(3) the person is deemed to have knowledge of the nature of the payment and that it was received at a criminal rate` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the person receives a payment or partial payment of interest at a criminal rate`
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a person receives a payment or partial payment of interest at a criminal rate" (a "Where" gate unmet: ruling of 2026-11-05 (b))
        IF `there is evidence to the contrary`
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "he shall, in the absence of evidence to the contrary, be deemed to have knowledge of the nature of the payment and that it was received at a criminal rate"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:6813 | Proof of annual percentage rate
-- src:6814 | (4) In any proceedings under this section, a certificate of a Fellow of the Canadian Institute of Actuaries stating that they have calculated the annual percentage rate of interest on any credit advanced and setting out the calculations and the information on which they are based is, in the absence of evidence to the contrary, proof of the annual percentage rate of interest without proof of the signature or official character of the person appearing to have signed the certificate.
@ref Criminal Code s 347(4) (src:6813-6814)
GIVEN `the proceedings are proceedings under section 347` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the document is a certificate of a Fellow of the Canadian Institute of Actuaries` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it states that they have calculated the annual percentage rate of interest on any credit advanced` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it sets out the calculations and the information on which they are based` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there is evidence to the contrary` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 347(4) the certificate is proof of the annual percentage rate of interest without proof of the signature or official character of the person appearing to have signed it` MEANS
    IF    `the proceedings are proceedings under section 347`
      AND `the document is a certificate of a Fellow of the Canadian Institute of Actuaries`
      AND `it states that they have calculated the annual percentage rate of interest on any credit advanced`
      AND `it sets out the calculations and the information on which they are based`
    THEN IF `there is evidence to the contrary`
         THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "is, in the absence of evidence to the contrary, proof of the annual percentage rate of interest"
         ELSE JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection speaks of a certificate of a Fellow of the Canadian Institute of Actuaries, in proceedings under section 347, that states the calculation and sets out the calculations and information

-- src:6815 | Notice
-- src:6816 | (5) A certificate referred to in subsection (4) shall not be received in evidence unless the party intending to produce it has given to the accused or defendant reasonable notice of that intention together with a copy of the certificate.
@ref Criminal Code s 347(5) (src:6815-6816)
GIVEN `the party intending to produce the certificate has given to the accused or defendant reasonable notice of that intention` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the party has given to the accused or defendant a copy of the certificate` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 347(5) the certificate may be received in evidence` MEANS
    IF `the party intending to produce the certificate has given to the accused or defendant reasonable notice of that intention` AND `the party has given to the accused or defendant a copy of the certificate`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "unless" met: the subsection stops barring the certificate but does not say that it shall be received (fork F-UNLESS)
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A certificate referred to in subsection (4) shall not be received in evidence unless the party intending to produce it has given to the accused or defendant reasonable notice of that intention together with a copy of the certificate"

-- src:6817 | Cross-examination with leave
-- src:6818 | (6) An accused or a defendant against whom a certificate referred to in subsection (4) is produced may, with leave of the court, require the attendance of the actuary for the purposes of cross-examination.
@ref Criminal Code s 347(6) (src:6817-6818)
GIVEN `a certificate referred to in subsection (4) is produced against the accused or defendant` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court has given leave` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 347(6) the accused or defendant may require the attendance of the actuary for the purposes of cross-examination` MEANS
    IF `a certificate referred to in subsection (4) is produced against the accused or defendant` AND `the court has given leave`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): a power "with leave of the court" for an accused or defendant against whom a certificate is produced; without leave the subsection grants nothing and denies nothing

-- src:6819 | (7) [Repealed, 2024, c. 17, s. 336]
@ref Criminal Code s 347(7) (src:6819)
`s 347(7) as the text shows it` MEANS "(7) [Repealed, 2024, c. 17, s. 336]"

-- src:6820 | Application
-- src:6821 | (8) This section does not apply to any transaction to which the Tax Rebate Discounting Act applies.
@ref Criminal Code s 347(8) (src:6820-6821)
GIVEN `the Tax Rebate Discounting Act applies to the transaction` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 347(8) section 347 applies to the transaction` MEANS
    IF `the Tax Rebate Discounting Act applies to the transaction`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This section does not apply to any transaction to which the Tax Rebate Discounting Act applies"
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection speaks only of a transaction to which that Act applies (a fact the Act, outside the sources, decides)

§§ `Section 347.01 -- non-application`

-- src:6822 | Non-application — agreements or arrangements
-- src:6823 | 347.01 (1) Section 347 does not apply in respect of agreements or arrangements provided for by regulation or in respect of offers, or advertisements of offers, provided for by regulation, to enter into an agreement or arrangement.
@ref Criminal Code s 347.01(1) (src:6822-6823)
GIVEN `the agreement or arrangement is provided for by regulation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the offer, or advertisement of an offer, to enter into an agreement or arrangement is provided for by regulation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 347.01(1) section 347 applies to the agreement, arrangement, offer or advertisement` MEANS
    IF `the agreement or arrangement is provided for by regulation` OR `the offer, or advertisement of an offer, to enter into an agreement or arrangement is provided for by regulation`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Section 347 does not apply in respect of agreements or arrangements provided for by regulation or in respect of offers, or advertisements of offers, provided for by regulation"
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): what the regulation provides for is outside the sources, and outside it the section says nothing

-- src:6824 | Non-application — offers and advertisements
-- src:6825 | (2) Section 347 also does not apply in respect of offers, or advertisements of offers, to enter into an agreement or arrangement if, had the agreement or arrangement been entered into, it would have been considered to be provided for by regulation.
@ref Criminal Code s 347.01(2) (src:6824-6825)
GIVEN `had the agreement or arrangement been entered into, it would have been considered to be provided for by regulation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 347.01(2) section 347 applies to the offer or advertisement of an offer` MEANS
    IF `had the agreement or arrangement been entered into, it would have been considered to be provided for by regulation`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Section 347 also does not apply in respect of offers, or advertisements of offers, to enter into an agreement or arrangement if, had the agreement or arrangement been entered into, it would have been considered to be provided for by regulation"
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection says no only where the agreement would have been provided for by regulation

§§ `Section 347.1 -- payday loans`

-- (1): "The following definitions apply in subsection (2)." interest has the same meaning as in subsection 347(2); payday loan means ...
-- src:6832 | interest has the same meaning as in subsection 347(2). (intérêts)
@ref Criminal Code s 347.1(1) interest (src:6832)
GIVEN `the aggregate of all charges and expenses, in any form, paid or payable for the advancing of credit under the agreement or arrangement, in dollars` IS A NUMBER
      `the part of it that is repayment of credit advanced, in dollars` IS A NUMBER
      `the part of it that is an insurance charge, in dollars` IS A NUMBER
      `the part of it that is an official fee, in dollars` IS A NUMBER
      `the part of it that is an overdraft charge, in dollars` IS A NUMBER
      `the part of it that is a required deposit balance, in dollars` IS A NUMBER
      `the transaction is a mortgage or hypothec transaction` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the part of it that is an amount required to be paid on account of property taxes, in dollars` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 347.1(1) interest` MEANS
    `s 347(2) interest`
        `the aggregate of all charges and expenses, in any form, paid or payable for the advancing of credit under the agreement or arrangement, in dollars`
        `the part of it that is repayment of credit advanced, in dollars`
        `the part of it that is an insurance charge, in dollars`
        `the part of it that is an official fee, in dollars`
        `the part of it that is an overdraft charge, in dollars`
        `the part of it that is a required deposit balance, in dollars`
        `the transaction is a mortgage or hypothec transaction`
        `the part of it that is an amount required to be paid on account of property taxes, in dollars`

-- src:6833 | payday loan means an advancement of money in exchange for a post-dated cheque, a pre-authorized debit or a future payment of a similar nature but not for any guarantee, suretyship, overdraft protection or security on property and not through a margin loan, pawnbroking, a line of credit or a credit card. (prêt sur salaire)
@ref Criminal Code s 347.1(1) payday loan (src:6833)
GIVEN `it is an advancement of money` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is in exchange for a post-dated cheque, a pre-authorized debit or a future payment of a similar nature` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is for a guarantee, suretyship, overdraft protection or security on property` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is made through a margin loan, pawnbroking, a line of credit or a credit card` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 347.1(1) the advancement of money is a payday loan` MEANS
    IF    `it is an advancement of money`
      AND `it is in exchange for a post-dated cheque, a pre-authorized debit or a future payment of a similar nature`
      AND NOT `it is for a guarantee, suretyship, overdraft protection or security on property`
      AND NOT `it is made through a margin loan, pawnbroking, a line of credit or a credit card`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "payday loan means an advancement of money in exchange for a post-dated cheque, a pre-authorized debit or a future payment of a similar nature but not for any guarantee, suretyship, overdraft protection or security on property and not through a margin loan, pawnbroking, a line of credit or a credit card"

-- (2): not a financial institution within the meaning of paragraphs (a) to (d) of the definition in section 2 of the Bank Act (outside the sources: an input);
-- the limit in (a.1) is fixed by regulation under (2.1) (outside the sources: the person states whether the total cost of borrowing is within it); the designation in (c) is by order under (3) (an input).
-- src:6834 | Non-application — person
-- src:6835 | (2) Section 347 and section 2 of the Interest Act do not apply to a person, other than a financial institution within the meaning of paragraphs (a) to (d) of the definition financial institution in section 2 of the Bank Act, who has entered into or has offered to enter into a payday loan agreement to receive interest, has advertised an offer to enter into a payday loan agreement that provides for the receipt of interest or has received interest under a payday loan agreement, if
-- src:6836 | (a) the amount of money that is or would be advanced under the agreement is $1,500 or less and the term of the agreement is or would be 62 days or less;
-- src:6837 | (a.1) the total cost of borrowing under the agreement does not or would not exceed the limit fixed by regulation;
-- src:6838 | (b) the person is licensed or otherwise specifically authorized under the laws of a province to enter into the agreement; and
-- src:6839 | (c) the province is designated under subsection (3).
@ref Criminal Code s 347.1(2) (src:6834-6839)
GIVEN `the person is a financial institution within the meaning of paragraphs (a) to (d) of the definition financial institution in section 2 of the Bank Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has entered into or has offered to enter into a payday loan agreement to receive interest, has advertised an offer to enter into a payday loan agreement that provides for the receipt of interest, or has received interest under a payday loan agreement` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the amount of money that is or would be advanced under the agreement, in dollars` IS A NUMBER
      `the term of the agreement, in days` IS A NUMBER
      `the total cost of borrowing under the agreement does not or would not exceed the limit fixed by regulation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is licensed or otherwise specifically authorized under the laws of a province to enter into the agreement` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the province is designated under subsection (3)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 347.1(2) section 347 and section 2 of the Interest Act apply to the person` MEANS
    IF    NOT `the person is a financial institution within the meaning of paragraphs (a) to (d) of the definition financial institution in section 2 of the Bank Act`
      AND `the person has entered into or has offered to enter into a payday loan agreement to receive interest, has advertised an offer to enter into a payday loan agreement that provides for the receipt of interest, or has received interest under a payday loan agreement`
      AND `the amount of money that is or would be advanced under the agreement, in dollars` AT MOST 1500
      AND `the term of the agreement, in days` AT MOST 62
      AND `the total cost of borrowing under the agreement does not or would not exceed the limit fixed by regulation`
      AND `the person is licensed or otherwise specifically authorized under the laws of a province to enter into the agreement`
      AND `the province is designated under subsection (3)`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Section 347 and section 2 of the Interest Act do not apply to a person, other than a financial institution within the meaning of paragraphs (a) to (d) of the definition financial institution in section 2 of the Bank Act, who has entered into or has offered to enter into a payday loan agreement to receive interest"
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection says no only where (a), (a.1), (b) and (c) all hold; where one fails it does not say that section 347 applies (fork F-NEG-IF)

-- 347.1(2.1) (the power to fix the limit by regulation) is machinery (inert, reason 2); its figure is an input of 347.1(2)(a.1).

-- src:6842 | Clarification
-- src:6843 | (2.2) If section 347 does not apply to a person by reason of subsection (2) immediately before a regulation made under subsection (2.1) comes into force, that section continues not to apply to the person if the total cost of borrowing under the agreement did not exceed the limit that applied immediately before the regulation came into force.
@ref Criminal Code s 347.1(2.2) (src:6842-6843)
GIVEN `section 347 did not apply to the person by reason of subsection (2) immediately before a regulation made under subsection (2.1) came into force` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the total cost of borrowing under the agreement did not exceed the limit that applied immediately before the regulation came into force` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 347.1(2.2) section 347 applies to the person` MEANS
    IF    `section 347 did not apply to the person by reason of subsection (2) immediately before a regulation made under subsection (2.1) came into force`
      AND `the total cost of borrowing under the agreement did not exceed the limit that applied immediately before the regulation came into force`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "that section continues not to apply to the person if the total cost of borrowing under the agreement did not exceed the limit that applied immediately before the regulation came into force"
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection says no only where section 347 did not apply under (2) just before the regulation and the cost did not exceed the earlier limit

-- src:6844 | Designation of province
-- src:6845 | (3) The Governor in Council shall, by order and at the request of the lieutenant governor in council of a province, designate the province for the purposes of this section if the province has legislative measures that protect recipients of payday loans and that provide for limits on the total cost of borrowing under the agreements.
@ref Criminal Code s 347.1(3) (src:6844-6845)
GIVEN `the lieutenant governor in council of the province has requested the designation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the province has legislative measures that protect recipients of payday loans` IS A BOOLEAN
      `those measures provide for limits on the total cost of borrowing under the agreements` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 347.1(3) the Governor in Council shall designate the province` MEANS
    IF    `the lieutenant governor in council of the province has requested the designation`
      AND `the province has legislative measures that protect recipients of payday loans`
      AND `those measures provide for limits on the total cost of borrowing under the agreements`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The Governor in Council shall, by order and at the request of the lieutenant governor in council of a province, designate the province for the purposes of this section if the province has legislative measures that protect recipients of payday loans and that provide for limits on the total cost of borrowing under the agreements" (a duty whose gate is unmet: fork F-DUTY)

-- src:6846 | Revocation
-- src:6847 | (4) The Governor in Council shall, by order, revoke the designation made under subsection (3) if requested to do so by the lieutenant governor in council of the province or if the legislative measures described in that subsection are no longer in force in that province.
@ref Criminal Code s 347.1(4) (src:6846-6847)
GIVEN `the lieutenant governor in council of the province has requested the revocation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the legislative measures described in subsection (3) are no longer in force in that province` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 347.1(4) the Governor in Council shall revoke the designation` MEANS
    IF `the lieutenant governor in council of the province has requested the revocation` OR `the legislative measures described in subsection (3) are no longer in force in that province`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The Governor in Council shall, by order, revoke the designation made under subsection (3) if requested to do so by the lieutenant governor in council of the province or if the legislative measures described in that subsection are no longer in force in that province" (a duty whose gate is unmet: fork F-DUTY)
